<section class="architecture" id="architecture">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-header">
      <p class="section-label">Architecture</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">How it's built</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="arch-stack">
      <div class="arch-layer">
        <div class="layer-head">
          <h3>Confidential container</h3>
          <span class="layer-tag">Runtime</span>
        </div>
        <p>The Hermes agent runs inside a confidential container on AMD SEV-SNP hardware. The entire VM memory is encrypted by the AMD Secure Processor — the hypervisor, the host OS, and the cloud provider cannot read what's inside. Remote attestation verifies the container is running genuine, unmodified code.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="arch-layer">
        <div class="layer-head">
          <h3>Persistent encrypted storage</h3>
          <span class="layer-tag">State</span>
        </div>
        <p>The agent maintains persistent state across sessions — conversation history, knowledge base, preferences, and context. All storage is encrypted and sealed to the enclave, so only the attested container can read it. Data survives restarts without ever being exposed.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="arch-layer">
        <div class="layer-head">
          <h3>Confidential inference</h3>
          <span class="layer-tag">LLM backend</span>
        </div>
        <p>All LLM queries go through confidential inference. Your prompts are encrypted before they reach the model provider, and responses are encrypted before they return. The provider sees ciphertext in and ciphertext out — they never see your prompts, context, or outputs.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="arch-layer">
        <div class="layer-head">
          <h3>Tool integration</h3>
          <span class="layer-tag">Interface</span>
        </div>
        <p>External services, data sources, and tools connected through encrypted channels. All communication exits the enclave encrypted, ensuring no data leakage to third parties.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .architecture {
    padding: 8rem 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #1A1A1D;
  }

  .section-inner {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .section-header {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #555558;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .section-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #F5F5F5;
  }

  .arch-stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .arch-layer {
    padding: 2rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #1A1A1D;
  }

  .arch-stack > :first-child {
    border-top: 1px solid #1A1A1D;
  }

  .layer-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .layer-head h3 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #F5F5F5;
  }

  .layer-tag {
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #555558;
  }

  .arch-layer p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #8A8A8E;
    max-width: 36rem;
  }

  .specs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .specs {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .spec {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.375rem;
  }

  .spec-label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #555558;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .spec-value {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: #F5F5F5;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .architecture { padding: 5rem 1.25rem; }
    .section-header { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .arch-layer { padding: 1.5rem 0; }
    .specs { gap: 1.25rem; }
  }
</style>
